.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Represents a mathematical 2D canvas storing color values of type \fIT\fP \&. This interface defines a deterministic data structure that models a rectangular grid of values\&. The canvas does not perform graphical drawing; instead, it provides structured access, mutation, and region‑based operations on its underlying data\&. 

All operations are purely mathematical and affect only the internal buffer\&. Visual output is never produced directly; color values are only observable through \fBGetPixel\fP, \fBBuffer\fP, or by transferring computed data into another canvas\&.

.PP
\fBTemplate Parameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIT\fP The color type stored in the canvas\&.
.RE
.PP

